# Aeris — secrets. gitignored, chmod 600. Never read by the browser.
# The Python server holds these; the page only ever sees text and audio bytes.

ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Voice. Default is Jessica — young, warm, confident.
# Audition and switch live from the UI (gear icon) — it writes back here.
#   Jessica  cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9   sweet + confident, American      <- default
#   Lily     pFZP5JQG7iQjIQuC4Bku   warm, British, steady
#   Alice    Xb7hH8MSUJpSbSDYk0k2   crisp, British, very confident
#   Matilda  XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX   soft, friendly, American
#   Sarah    EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL   gentle, low, American
#   Laura    FGY2WhTYpPnrIDTdsKH5   bright, upbeat, American
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9
ELEVENLABS_TTS_MODEL=eleven_turbo_v2_5
ELEVENLABS_STT_MODEL=scribe_v1

# Voice character. 0..1 each.
ELEVENLABS_STABILITY=0.42
ELEVENLABS_SIMILARITY=0.80
ELEVENLABS_STYLE=0.35
ELEVENLABS_SPEED=1.03

# 1 = invented fixtures, safe to screen-record.  0 = your real folders.
# Read in exactly one file: agent/data.py
AERIS_DEMO=1

# Your real folders, used only when AERIS_DEMO=0. Colon-separated. Read-only.
AERIS_VAULT_ROOTS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the brain
# "auto" uses whatever is reachable, cheapest first. All three are tried:
#
#   ollama      local, free, fast, and the weakest reasoning
#   claude_cli  the `claude` command you already have. FREE — it runs on your
#               Claude subscription, so a turn costs nothing extra. This is
#               the one that makes Aeris good without making her metered.
#   anthropic   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. PAID, per token, and billed SEPARATELY
#               from your subscription. Leave it blank to stay free.
#
# Routine turns prefer Ollama for speed; thinking prefers Claude.
AERIS_LLM=auto
OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.1
CLAUDE_CLI=claude
CLAUDE_CLI_MODEL=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the voice
# Both default to the free local option when it is available.
#
#   AERIS_TTS=auto|macos|elevenlabs|off
#     macos       the `say` command. Free, instant, no setup. Better voices
#                 are a download away in System Settings > Accessibility >
#                 Spoken Content > System Voice > Manage Voices.
#     elevenlabs  much better, and billed per character.
#
#   AERIS_STT=auto|whisper|elevenlabs|off
#     whisper     free and local, and genuinely excellent on Apple Silicon.
#                 Needs: brew install whisper-cpp ffmpeg, then point
#                 WHISPER_MODEL at a downloaded ggml model file.
#     elevenlabs  Scribe. Metered.
AERIS_TTS=auto
AERIS_STT=auto

# The wake word. Press the wake button and the mic stays shut to her until she
# hears this — audio is watched locally, and nothing is sent or kept until it
# matches. Wake mode REFUSES to run on ElevenLabs: it would transcribe every
# sentence spoken near your desk and bill you for each one. Install the free
# local whisper above and it switches itself on.
AERIS_WAKE_WORD=aeris
MACOS_VOICE=Samantha
MACOS_RATE=
WHISPER_BIN=
WHISPER_MODEL=
WHISPER_LANGUAGE=en

# --------------------------------------------------------------- her hands
# Folders Aeris may write in, colon-separated. Empty means she writes nothing
# and says so. Everything she overwrites is copied into .aeris-backups/ first,
# and every action is appended to Aeris/audit/actions.jsonl.
#
# Deleting, running commands, and touching .env or agent/ always stop and ask,
# whatever is set here.
AERIS_WRITE_ROOTS=

# Where new notes she writes land. Defaults to your first vault root, so
# captures join the graph you already have. Must sit inside AERIS_WRITE_ROOTS.
AERIS_CAPTURE_DIR=

# Memory can live inside an Obsidian vault, so her notes and yours are one
# graph. Defaults to Aeris/memory.
AERIS_MEMORY_DIR=

# Free local embeddings, which is what makes memory recall find a thing you
# phrased differently. ollama pull nomic-embed-text
OLLAMA_EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text
OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL=llama3.2-vision

# Web research. Optional. Without it, research_web says so out loud.
AERIS_WEB_SEARCH=duckduckgo

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ github
# Free. github.com/settings/tokens — a fine-grained token with read access to
# your repositories is enough for everything except opening issues, and
# opening an issue stops and asks you anyway.
#
# Leave GITHUB_REPOS blank and Aeris lists your repositories herself. A
# fine-grained token limited to selected repositories cannot do that (GitHub
# returns 403 on the account-wide endpoint, which is correct, not a bug) — so
# name them here instead and each is fetched directly.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
GITHUB_REPOS=

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- railway
# Free. railway.com/account/tokens.
#
# Read-only — Aeris can tell you what is broken, deploying or live, and cannot
# redeploy or restart anything.
#
# Two kinds of token authenticate differently, and sending the wrong header is
# a 401 that looks like a bad token. An account or workspace token uses
# Authorization: Bearer and sees everything. A token scoped to one project
# uses a different header entirely — set RAILWAY_TOKEN_TYPE=project for that.
# Leave it on auto unless you get a 401.
#
# Verify it before trusting it:  python3 -m agent.railway
RAILWAY_TOKEN=
RAILWAY_TOKEN_TYPE=auto

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ notion
# Free. notion.so/my-integrations — create an internal integration and copy
# its secret. Then, and this is the step everyone misses: open each page you
# want Aeris to read, ... menu, Connections, add your integration. Notion
# shows an integration nothing by default.
#
# Read-only. Verify with:  python3 -m agent.notion
NOTION_TOKEN=

# ------------------------------------------------ gmail + calendar (google)
# Free, but the only connector here that costs you real setup time, because
# Google has no personal access tokens. Roughly twenty minutes, once:
#
#   1. console.cloud.google.com — create a project
#   2. APIs & Services > Library — enable "Gmail API" and "Google Calendar API"
#   3. APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen — External, add yourself as a
#      test user (it never needs verifying while you are the only user)
#   4. APIs & Services > Credentials > Create credentials > OAuth client ID
#      Application type: DESKTOP APP
#   5. Paste the client ID and secret below
#   6. Run: python3 -m agent.google authorize
#
# Scopes are read-only unless you opt in below. Google bundles drafting and
# sending into one scope, so drafts are off by default — and even with them
# on, Aeris has no send function at all. A draft sits in your drafts folder
# until you send it yourself.
#
# Verify with:  python3 -m agent.google
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_ALLOW_DRAFTS=
# Adding a calendar event is visible immediately — unlike a draft, there is
# nothing to review first. It still always stops and asks before saving one,
# and there is no way for it to invite anyone: only he can do that, in
# Calendar itself. Re-run `python3 -m agent.google authorize` after changing
# this — new scopes only take effect on a fresh sign-in.
GOOGLE_ALLOW_CALENDAR_WRITE=

PORT=4719
